The last guide-side screen the API supported is in: guides can post and manage updates. The endpoint pair was already wired in the repository but had no UI, so I built the composer and the feed around it.

**Updates tab** — [guide_shell.dart](mobile/lib/features/guide_tools/guide_shell.dart) now has a fourth tab listing `GET /guide/status` newest-first: a type chip, the message, a subtitle resolving the linked listing to its title (`All experiences` when unlinked), area, date, `6/8 spots`, and a relative age like `3 h ago`. Deleting asks first and refetches; a failed delete leaves the row in place with the server's message. It's the same shape as the Requests/Listings tabs, so it inherits their loading, error and empty states.

**Composer** — [guide_status_composer_screen.dart](mobile/lib/features/guide_tools/guide_status_composer_screen.dart) at `/guide/status/new` posts one update. It shows only the fields that mean something for the chosen type — capacity numbers for `capacity`, a date picker for `schedule` — because `GuideStatusCreate` accepts all of them freely and a form that always shows four irrelevant boxes invites junk data. The listing picker is optional, and if the guide's listings can't be loaded the update still posts guide-wide rather than dead-ending.

**Validation** in `GuideStatusDraft` ([guide_models.dart](mobile/lib/features/guide_tools/guide_models.dart)) mirrors the server: message 3–2000, area 160, capacities 0/1–1000. It also enforces `booked <= total`, which the server does *not* cross-check, so that particular error can only be caught client-side. A `listing_id` the guide doesn't own comes back 404 — surfaced inline with the drafted text intact instead of detaching silently.

**One layout bug found and fixed:** the dashboard stat grid used a fixed `childAspectRatio` that overflowed by 14 px at 360 dp width, and would again at larger text scales. It's now two rows of content-sized cells equalised with `IntrinsicHeight`, so the value + label always fit.

**Verified:** `flutter analyze` → No issues found; `flutter test` → **108/108 passed** (19 new in [guide_status_test.dart](mobile/test/guide_status_test.dart), plus a `Formatters.relativeTime` case in [widget_test.dart](mobile/test/widget_test.dart)); `flutter build apk --debug` → built. The new tests drive the real forms — capacity fields appearing and required, the actual `showDatePicker` producing an ISO `event_date`, a listing chip producing `listing_id: 4`, a 404 keeping the text, and the feed's delete confirmation. Route guarding for `/guide/status/new` is covered in [app_router_redirect_test.dart](mobile/test/app_router_redirect_test.dart).

Two caveats worth being explicit about. The 360 dp overflow test clears exceptions raised by the Overview first, because Flutter's test font renders every glyph a full em wide and inflates button labels ~2×; the assertion covers the tab I added, not the whole screen at that width. And these updates are workspace-only — nothing outside `/guide/status` reads the rows, so the composer says "not shown to travellers yet" rather than implying a feed exists. I documented that, the listing-ownership 404, and the client-side `booked <= total` rule in [api-gaps.md](mobile/docs/api-gaps.md) and [api-integration.md](mobile/docs/api-integration.md), and refreshed [architecture.md](mobile/docs/architecture.md), [testing.md](mobile/docs/testing.md) (now with all ten suites listed) and the README gates. Nothing is committed.

The obvious next move is making this data actually reach travellers, since three capabilities now sit behind one missing backend join.
