**What changed** — [home_shell.dart:173-218](mobile/lib/features/home/home_shell.dart#L173-L218), the `_localUpdatesHeader` method:

- The header previously was just a plain `Text('Updates in $homeCity')`. It now shows a live count badge beside the title: a pill-shaped chip (matching the app's existing `surfacePeach` / `radiusPill` style) displaying how many updates the selected city currently has.
- The count is read from the same `cityUpdatesProvider(homeCity)` instance that the section below renders, so there's no second network request and no chance the badge disagrees with the list it labels. It hides itself while loading, on error, and when the city has no updates — so it never claims a number it doesn't have.
- The title is now ellipsized inside a `Flexible` instead of overflowing when the city name runs long, and the "Change" row got `mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min` so it hugs its label.

Along the way Flutter's analyzer caught one issue in my first draft (`error: (_, _)` reuses `_`, which isn't allowed) — fixed by naming the parameters.

