The signed-in screens finally have pixels — and reviewing them found real defects.

**A repeatable capture harness** — [design_capture_test.dart](mobile/test/design_capture_test.dart) renders the real screens with the real theme, the bundled Inter/Playfair/MaterialIcons fonts, a scripted transport and a 390×844 viewport (status-bar inset included), then writes PNGs to [docs/screens/](mobile/docs/screens). It is skipped unless you pass `--dart-define=CAPTURE_SCREENS=true`, so the normal suite gains nothing to flake on.

**Four defects the review caught, all fixed**

1. **The "Guest favourite" ribbon slid under the save heart** on two-up grid cards — the heart literally covered the end of the word. It now sits at the photo's bottom-left on every card, one corner the heart never occupies, so the label stays whole. Squeezing it into the remaining top width instead produced "Guest favou…", which was worse.
2. **"14 h ago"** — hours were the only unit abbreviated after a space, so it read as a typo next to "12 min ago" and "4 days ago". Now "14 hr ago" everywhere.
